P5. Families met in the census (exact checks):
    tau(1,3,12k) = 5/12 + 1/(48k), k = 1..200: OK (proved in P2)
    Safe_(1/5)(1,3,4) cap [0,1/2] = {1/5}, [2/5,9/20]
    tau(1,3,4,5k) = 2/5 + 1/(25k), k = 1..200: OK  [5k kills 1/5 and 2/5 (multiples of 1/5);
     the next safe point of 5k after 2/5 is (2k+1/5)/(5k) = 2/5 + 1/(25k), inside [2/5,9/20]]

==============================================================================
P6. Good period q(v): two easy facts.
    (a) q is UNBOUNDED for every n >= 2: if L = lcm(1..Q) is a speed, every t = k/q with
        q <= Q has ||L t|| = 0, so q(v) > Q (e.g. v = (1, L) is primitive).
    (b) q(v) <= 2 vmax whenever LRC holds for v: delta is attained at some t* = m/(v_i+v_j)
        (A1), f(t*) = delta >= 1/(n+1), so t* is a good time with denominator <= v_i+v_j <= 2vmax.
    (c) den(tau) >= q(v) always (tau is itself a good time).
    (a) exact: Q=2: q(1,2)=3; Q=3: q(1,6)=5; Q=4: q(1,12)=8; Q=5: q(1,60)=8; Q=6: q(1,60)=8; Q=7: q(1,420)=8; Q=8: q(1,840)=9; Q=9: q(1,2520)=11; Q=10: q(1,2520)=11; Q=11: q(1,27720)=13; Q=12: q(1,27720)=13
    (b) exact check q(v) <= 2 vmax on the required universes: OK; max q/vmax: n=2: 5/3 at (2, 3) (q=5); n=3: 7/4 at (1, 3, 4) (q=7); n=4: 9/5 at (1, 3, 4, 5) (q=9); n=5: 5/3 at (1, 2, 4, 5, 6) (q=10)

